libroger display shaders
========================

    build.py vendor DIR   copy what the chains need from a checkout of
                          https://github.com/libretro/slang-shaders into slang/
    build.py [NAME...]    compile the chains (all, or those named) into
                          generated/chains.c (needs glslang; GLSLANG=path)
    slangp.py             reading presets and shaders (includes, passes)
    own/                  libroger's own shaders and presets
    slang/                shaders from slang-shaders, unmodified, at the
                          revision in slang/UPSTREAM
    generated/chains.c    SPIR-V, uniform and sampler tables and lookup
                          textures (PNG) for src/shader.c - committed, so
                          building libroger doesn't need glslang

The chains, in F10 order (build.py's CHAINS):

    name                 preset                                       licence
    bilinear             own/bilinear.slangp                          libroger
    lanczos3             interpolation/lanczos3-fast.slangp           GPL-2.0+
    spline36             interpolation/spline36-fast.slangp           GPL-2.0+
    xbr-lv2              edge-smoothing/xbr/xbr-lv2.slangp            MIT (Hyllian)
    xbrz                 edge-smoothing/xbrz/xbrz-freescale-multipass MIT (Hyllian) + GPL-3.0 (Zenju's xBRZ)
    scalefx              edge-smoothing/scalefx/scalefx.slangp        MIT (Sp00kyFox)
    crt                  own/crt.slangp                               libroger
    crt-lottes           crt/crt-lottes.slangp                        public domain (Timothy Lottes)
    crt-hyllian          crt/crt-hyllian-fast.slangp                  MIT (Hyllian)
    crt-geom             crt/crt-geom.slangp                          GPL-2.0+ (cgwg, Themaister, DOLLS)
    crt-easymode         crt/crt-easymode.slangp                      GPL (EasyMode; no version given)
    crt-guest-advanced   crt/crt-guest-advanced.slangp                GPL-2.0+ (guest(r))
    crt-royale           crt/crt-royale.slangp                        GPL-2.0+ (TroggleMonkey); MIT helpers

Together that makes libroger's shaders GPL-3.0 (xBRZ is GPL-3.0, the
others GPL-2.0-or-later or permissive); leaving xbrz out of CHAINS would
leave GPL-2.0-or-later.

Each file in slang/ keeps its own copyright and licence notice; the MIT
notices are part of what must accompany a binary. Files slang-shaders has
without a licence notice are not used: stock.slang and xBR's
linearize/delinearize are replaced by own/stock.slang, own/linearize.slang
and own/delinearize.slang (build.py's REPLACE), and crt-hyllian uses the
single-pass "fast" preset rather than the one with unlicensed glow passes.

How a slang shader becomes a pair of SDL_GPU shaders (build.py's convert()):
the stages are split at #pragma stage; the push-constant block and the UBO
are merged into one uniform block (vertex set 1, fragment set 3, binding 0),
also reachable through the old instance names (#define params rs); samplers
are renumbered (fragment set 2 with Source at 0, vertex set 0); #pragma
parameter / name / format become table entries. src/shader.c fills the
block per pass (sizes, FrameCount, parameters with the preset's values)
and keeps what the presets ask for: pass outputs by alias, feedback,
history, mipmapped inputs, float / sRGB targets, absolute / source /
viewport scaling, lookup textures. Not supported: clamp_to_border (taken as
clamp_to_edge; SDL_GPU has no border colour), runtime parameter changes.
